course: dictionary
lesson: 15594
title: Words you can feel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tactile is a word about touch. Something tactile can be felt with your fingers or your skin. The clue is in the sound of the word: tactile starts with tact, like touch.
explain: «The tactile paving at the road crossing has bumpy dots.» People who cannot see well can feel those bumps under their feet, so they know where the crossing is. The bumps are tactile because they can be felt by touching.
explain: Tactile can also describe something nice to touch: «The soft clay is very tactile.» A tactile person likes to touch other people a lot, for example by hugging or patting them. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does «Sam is a tactile person» still make sense with touch in it? It does.
fact: Tactile means about the sense of touch, or able to be felt by touching.
fact: «Tactile paving» is the bumpy pavement at road crossings that helps blind and partially sighted people.
fact: Braille is a tactile way of reading, using raised dots that you feel with your fingers.
fact: A tactile learner learns best by touching and handling things.
fact: Touch is one of the five senses, along with sight, hearing, taste and smell.
exercise: «The soft clay is very tactile.» What does tactile mean here? | Loud and noisy | Cold to taste | Hard to see through | *Nice to touch
exercise: Tactile paving at a road crossing has bumpy dots. Why is it useful? | *People who cannot see well can feel it under their feet | It keeps the road dry | It makes the traffic lights change faster | It glows in the dark
exercise: Find the word that means able to be felt by touching. | bright | silent | sour | *tactile
test: «Sam is a tactile person, so he always gives his friends a hug.» What does tactile suggest about Sam? | Sam hates the dark | *Sam likes to touch and hug people | Sam cannot feel anything at all | Sam is afraid of loud noises
test: Mia is a tactile learner. What does that mean? | She learns by reading silently | *She learns best by touching and handling things | She never learns anything new | She learns only by listening
exam: «The sensory box was full of tactile materials, like sponge, sand and silk.» Which sense does tactile link to? | Taste | Hearing | *Touch | Smell
